  "$comment": "REVIEWED PROTECTION BASELINE. Records how strongly each rule is enforced: its level, whether it admits an exception, and its severity. scripts/integrity.mjs fails on any drift between this file and the catalog, which means weakening a rule requires editing this file too - a second, deliberate, reviewable act that appears in a diff on its own line. NEVER REGENERATE THIS FILE FROM A RUN. A --write flag would defeat the mechanism entirely, because the first response to a red build would be to run it. Edit by hand and record the reason in CHANGELOG.md naming the rule id. See standards/18-standards-integrity.md.",
